<title>JAPAN: MOF seen auctioning T-bills, 20-yr bonds next week.</title>
<headline>MOF seen auctioning T-bills, 20-yr bonds next week.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ministry of Finance (MOF) is likely to offer six-month Treasury bills and 20-year Japanese government bonds (JGBs) through price-competitive auctions next week, bond traders said on Friday.  </p>
<p>They said the T-bill auction is likely to be held on Monday and the 20-year JGB auction on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The T-bills will be auctioned for the MOF to roll over 1.5 trillion yen worth of six-month T-bills maturing on April 10, they said.</p>
<p>When the MOF last auctioned 20-year JGBs on January 21, it offered 400 billion yen of 3.3 percent bonds. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8570</p>
</text>
